  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Issue**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the user\'s interaction. Initially, they provided \"TESTE\" which led to a basic \"Test App\" setup. Now, the user is requesting a deeper dive with \"TESTE MEU APP E VEJA POSSIVEIS FALHAS E SOL\303\207\303\225ES\". I\'m focusing on how to proceed from the initial token to a full-blown failure analysis and solution generation, so that the response is more aligned to their current instructions.\n\n\n**Examining the Code**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the user\'s provided HTML code for \"PERFORT ALMOX - Controle de Estoque e Movimenta\303\247\303\243o.\" My current focus is to identify the application\'s core functionality, pinpoint any bugs or potential failures within the codebase, and determine the optimal approach: either fixing and serving the HTML directly or integrating/porting the application into a React/Vite structure for enhanced performance and maintainability.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Key Deficiencies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the specific architectural deficiencies found within the provided \"PERFORT ALMOX\" HTML code. I\'ve identified several syntax and reference errors, specifically within functions like `showPage()`, `renderDashboard()`, `openHeaderEditor()`, and `renderNotifList()`, including undefined functions and potential issues with uninitialized variables. This also includes checks on missing functions, as well as checking the values of the functions.\n\n\n**Identifying Critical Errors**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed crucial errors in the \"PERFORT ALMOX\" HTML. The script attempts to access non-existent elements like \'notif-panel\' and \'btn-notif\', causing a `TypeError`. The `renderRelatorio()` and `filtrarDashboard()` functions have potential failures due to uninitialized variables and chart object issues. Additionally, I\'ve found a critical undefined function, `ajustarMenuPorRole`, that will break `showApp()`. I\'m now verifying further element IDs within `addCQList`, `initCQSelects`, `buildCQSelect`, and inconsistencies in table structures within `renderCQ()`.\n\n\n**Uncovering More Issues**\n\nI\'m now identifying additional problems in \"PERFORT ALMOX.\" Specifically, there\'s a discrepancy between the expected table columns (17) and the columns in the `<tbody>`. I\'ve also identified issues related to external dependencies. `loadConfigCloudSync()` references undefined cloud configuration functions, while `exportarRelatorioPDF()` relies on external CDN libraries that might be blocked in certain environments. `initFirebaseSync()` dynamically imports Firebase, which can fail. Finally, `analisarEstoqueComIA()` and `sendIAMessage()` face import problems with the `@google/generative-ai` package, as well as an undefined import attempt.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Strategy**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the best approach to address the user\'s need, considering the provided application and the user\'s request for failure analysis and solutions. I\'m focusing on whether a direct HTML fix or a React conversion is the optimal path to ensure this is a production-ready application. I\'m currently assessing the risks and benefits of both options. I\'m also ensuring that I\'m aligned with their instructions.\n\n\n**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now defining the implementation strategy for \"PERFORT ALMOX.\" My plan is to convert the HTML app into a React app. This will involve a detailed report of the failures and implemented solutions. The React app will run flawlessly in a Vite preview. It preserves all functionality, including branding, authentication, multi-obra support, and business logic.\n\n\n**Mapping the Modules**\n\nI\'m currently mapping out the modules within \"PERFORT ALMOX.\" My focus is now on the core features, like `Obra` management with tenant data isolation, and `Insumo` management including item CRUD, automatic status calculations (OK, BAIXO, CR\303\215TICO). I\'m also ensuring the implementation of detailed entry and exit registers, including history, filtering, export options, and stock availability checks. I\'m focusing on defining the dynamic destination addition in exits.\n\n\n**Detailing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now detailing the dashboard features for \"PERFORT ALMOX.\" I\'m prioritizing the implementation of live KPI cards displaying vital metrics like total items, stock value, alert items, and monthly entries/exits. I\'m also focusing on the status KPIs (OK, Alerta, Cr\303\255tico counts, values, coverage rate, and average turnover). Additionally, I\'m ensuring the inclusion of charts (Status Distribution, Monthly Evolution, Top 10 Stock Value, Value by Family) and a filterable low stock table. A recent movements stream is also being implemented.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 22
      nanos: 278502241
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
